# EVERY SETTLED NODE UNDER A COMPOSED LAYER, WITH ITS REMAINDER CARRIED UP. One row per
# (composed layer, settled node) pair, the factors along the path already multiplied in.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ THIS IS THE RECURSION TAKEN AS A JOIN, AND THE STOPPING RULE IS THE WHOLE CONTENT. A
#    fusion's remainder is defined by recursion on `F`, and the natural form needs a SUM in the
#    recursive term, which SQL forbids. The recursion FLATTENS instead: substitute it into
#    itself and the intermediate layers cancel, leaving one sum with the factors multiplied
#    along each path. A running product is a scalar per row and IS allowed in a recursive term,
#    so composition/descent.sqlc's walk carries it and this is a join.
#
# ⛔⛔ IT STOPS AT THE FIRST SETTLED NODE AND NOT AT A LEAF, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS NOT AN
#    OPTIMISATION. A settled node's `n` and `d` were never scaled by one factor with width, so
#    differencing them is legitimate and its filed totals are a claim its composer stands
#    behind. Descend past one and those totals are bypassed, along with every correction that
#    composer already applied, which then has to be rebuilt from below and can fail for reasons
#    the filed figure had already settled. `merge-group-composition/compute-pt` is that case:
#    it files a demand, its own conversion is a point, and one of its eliminations is unsized.
#    Stopping there reads a figure; running past it reaches a correction nobody sized.
#
# ⭐ composition/unsettled.sqlc is the predicate, and a leaf satisfies it trivially by having
#   no parts at all. The leaf is the special case of the base case, not the base case.
#
# ⛔ THE CORNER RULE IS THE SAME ONE WITH THE PATH PRODUCT AS THE DRIVER: for a strictly
#   positive product the bounds are the two corners on each side, which collapses to the
#   component-wise form when the node's remainder is non-negative and reverses when it is not.
#
# ⚠️ `NOT w.is_cycle` HERE IS A GUARD AND NOT A DETECTOR. It keeps a looped path out of an
#   arithmetic and reports nothing about one. A document whose parts loop has no evaluation
#   order at all, and `checks/layers_move_together` is what says so; this relation simply declines to
#   return a number for it.
-- composition/remainder_frontier.sqlc less the nodes composition/unsettled.sqlc names,
-- against layers/differenced_remainder.sqlc at the node the walk stops on.
SELECT w.root_filing AS composition, w.root_layer AS composed_layer,
       w.filing AS node_filing, w.layer AS node_layer, w.depth,
       w.factor_low, w.factor_mode, w.factor_high,
       least(   r.r_low  * w.factor_low, r.r_low  * w.factor_high) AS r_low,
       r.r_mode * w.factor_mode                                    AS r_mode,
       greatest(r.r_high * w.factor_low, r.r_high * w.factor_high) AS r_high,
       (w.factor_low IS DISTINCT FROM w.factor_high)               AS spread_factor
FROM      (
    :compose(composition/remainder_frontier.sqlc)
) w
JOIN      (
    :compose(layers/differenced_remainder.sqlc)
) r ON r.filing = w.filing AND r.layer = w.layer
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(composition/unsettled.sqlc)
) o ON o.filing = w.filing AND o.layer = w.layer
WHERE w.factor_absent = false
  AND NOT w.is_cycle
  AND o.filing IS NULL
